  "intro": {
    "language": "en",
    "text": "Vicki Hollub (born 1959) is an American businesswoman and mineral engineer. She was president and chief executive officer of Occidental Petroleum from April 2016 to June 2026, when Richard Jackson succeeded her; she remained on the company's board after retiring as chief executive. She was the first woman to lead a major American oil company.",
    "sourceId": "wikipedia-en",
    "usage": "Research excerpt; paraphrase and cross-check before publication."
  },
